From: opencode <opencode@local>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:03:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] autograph: seven throats print CHIMERA in a 5x7 grid

An experiment, not a product feature: the engine signs its own name with seven
voices, one per row of the 5x7 font the plot tools already use. A voice sounds
wherever its glyph row has ink, so a horizontal stroke is a held note and a
vertical stroke is a chord. Pitches are a whole-tone cluster from G3 to G#4 so
no row is an octave from another; two male pedals and a small room carry the
mix.

The poster's grid is read back from the audio: RMS in each cell of each throat's
rendered stem. It recovers all 113 ink cells and all 174 rests with no false
onsets. `tools/autograph-poster.ts` draws the recovered grid;
`tools/autograph-player.ts` makes a self-contained player with a live spectrum.

Ran: cargo test -p chimera-cli (12 passed), render autograph (12.0 s, peak 0.900),
the poster and player in Node 24, and the standalone player in Chrome (audio
ready, 12 s, playhead and spectrum live).
